            {
              "text": "When resolving parenting arrangements and child custody disputes in Brisbane’s Western Suburbs (Indooroopilly and the Centenary area), you will generally need either **legal representation** (a family lawyer to advise and negotiate on your behalf) or an **Accredited Family Dispute Resolution Practitioner (FDRP)** (an independent mediator authorised to issue Section 60I certificates required by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia).\n\nSeveral reputable firms and practitioners based directly in or adjacent to Indooroopilly and the Centenary suburbs specialise in these matters:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Law Firms Based in Indooroopilly & Centenary Suburbs\n\n* **Littles Family Lawyers (Indooroopilly)**\n  * **Location:** Stamford Road / Station Road, Indooroopilly.\n  * **Focus:** Parenting agreements, child custody disputes, and alternative dispute resolution. \n  * **Why consider them:** They are one of the few dedicated boutique family law practices physically situated in the heart of Indooroopilly. Their team prioritises child-focused outcomes and keeping disputes out of court through structured settlement and mediation.\n* **Jindalee Lawyers (Centenary Suburbs)**\n  * **Location:** Sinnamon Road, Jindalee.\n  * **Focus:** Parenting plans, custody arrangements, consent orders, and community legal support across the Centenary suburbs (Jindalee, Mount Ommaney, Westlake, Sinnamon Park).\n  * **Why consider them:** As an established local practice in the Centenary area, they offer accessible, relationship-focused legal counsel. They are ideal if you want pragmatic, local legal advice to negotiate living arrangements without high inner-city firm overheads.\n* **Shearer Doyle Law / Doyle Family Law (Kenmore – adjacent to Indooroopilly & Centenary)**\n  * **Location:** Marshall Lane, Kenmore.\n  * **Focus:** Complex parenting disputes, child welfare, and dispute resolution.\n  * **Why consider them:** Principal Bruce Doyle is an Accredited Family Law Specialist, former President of the Family Law Practitioners Association of Queensland (FLPA), and a former Deputy President of the Queensland Children’s Services Tribunal. His depth of experience in high-conflict parenting disputes and child protection matters is among the highest in the western corridor.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Accredited Family Dispute Resolution Practitioners (Mediators) Serving the Area\n\nUnder the *Family Law Act 1975*, separated parents are generally required to make a genuine effort to resolve disputes through an accredited FDRP before filing in court. For mediation specifically:\n\n* **Amanda Kent – Resolve Family Law Mediations (Kenmore / Western Suburbs)**\n  * **Accreditation:** Registered FDRP (Attorney-General’s Department) & Family Lawyer.\n  * **Focus:** Facilitates parenting mediation and is legally authorized to issue Section 60I certificates. Experienced in navigating complex dynamics, including parental alienation, communication breakdowns, and domestic conflict.\n* **Dannielle Young – Family Mediation Brisbane (Servicing Western Suburbs / Centenary)**\n  * **Accreditation:** Registered FDRP & experienced former family lawyer.\n  * **Focus:** Child-focused mediation, shuttle mediation (where parents stay in separate rooms or online breakout rooms), parenting plans, and drafting terms for consent orders. Active in the Centenary business/community network.\n* **Shannon Daykin – Daykin Family Law (Servicing Indooroopilly & Western Suburbs)**\n  * **Accreditation:** QLS Accredited Family Law Specialist & Accredited FDRP / Mediator.\n  * **Focus:** Consistently recognised in *Doyle’s Guide* for Leading Parenting & Children's Matters Lawyers in Brisbane. Shannon provides both legal representation in child custody matters and independent mediation services for separating parents.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Community & Subsidised Dispute Resolution\n\nIf you are seeking community-funded or sliding-scale mediation near the Western Suburbs:\n* **Relationships Australia Queensland:** Regularly conducts FDR for parenting plans, child-inclusive mediation, and Section 60I assessments, with accessible appointments across Brisbane (in-person or telehealth).\n* **Centacare Family Dispute Resolution:** Provides low-cost, accredited parenting and custody mediation services across greater Brisbane.\n\n---\n\n### How to Choose the Right Practitioner\n\n1. **Representation vs. Mediation:** If you and your ex-partner both agree to mediate, you must engage an **independent FDRP** who cannot give either of you individual legal advice. If you need someone in your corner to advocate, negotiate, or draft court consent orders, you must engage your own **family lawyer**.\n2. **Section 60I Accreditation:** If your goal is to fulfill the court pre-action requirements (or obtain a 60I certificate because the other party refuses to participate), ensure the mediator is officially registered as an FDRP with the Commonwealth Attorney-General’s Department, not merely a commercial mediator.\n3. **Child-Inclusive Practice:** If your children are school-aged and the dispute involves living schedules or school choices, ask whether the mediator offers **Child-Inclusive Mediation**, where an independent child consultant speaks with the children and relays their developmental needs into the session.",
